For a unit cube (side length 1), we calculate the volume of the tetrahedron formed by the purple vertices. Using the scalar triple product formula for the volume of a tetrahedron with vertices \(\mathbf{v}_1, \mathbf{v}_2, \mathbf{v}_3, \mathbf{v}_4\):  
\[
\text{Volume} = \frac{1}{6} \left| \text{scalar triple product of vectors from one vertex to the others} \right|
